>My 1st level priest found a Wand of Wishing.  The first wish I think I
>did the smart thing by wishing for a blessed scroll of charging, then
>excalibur and gauntlets of power since he has strength of 9 and last
>gray dragon scale mail.  So I have 3 wish left right?

SPOILERS follow, of course.

You do know that you're allowed to wish for 3 scrolls or potions?  So
you could have wished for "3 belssed scrolls of charging" for example.
On weapons and armor you can wish for a +3 bonus, i.e. "blessed +3 gray
dragon scale mail."

Cursed scrolls of genocide would probably be a waste at this point,
where it's easy to get experience by killing things.  I usually don't
use them until the character is above experience level 15 or so.  If
you're really worried about hit points "3 blessed potions of gain
ability" might help by raising constitution.  But I probably wouldn't
do that either.

I'd probably use one or two immediately for better armor: "blessed +3
pair of speed boots" and maybe "blessed +3 cloak of invisibility" (or
maybe displacement).  The speed boots will be a big help in battles.

Other things you might want now are 3 blessed scrolls of identify or 3
blessed scrolls of enchant armor or weapon (but be careful).  Blessed
amulets of lifesaving are handy too.

You'll probably eventually want a magic marker, but right now you
probably don't know enough scrolls to get much use out of one, so it
might be worth waiting until you need it.  Ditto for the ring of
levitation; you probably won't need one until the castle level (where
there's another wand of wishing).  If you're unlucky and don't get a
blindfold before dungeon level 15 or so, you might even want to wish
for one of those before you run into Medusa.

Finally, when you've used up your remaining 3 wishes, keep trying to
zap the wand again.  It will keep saying "Nothing happens", but
eventually you will "wrest one more spell from the wand" or some such
thing.  It may take 50-100 tries.
